.TH "RECORD\-START\.SH" "" "June 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-start\.sh\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-start\.sh\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-start\.sh\fR launches \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR as a detached background process and records its PID for use by other RECORD workflow tools\. It sources \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR, which validates the environment and checks the PID file before any action is taken\.
.P
If \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR is already running (determined by the presence of a valid PID in the PID file and a live \fB/proc/<pid>\fR entry), the script writes a timestamped error to standard error and exits with status \-1 without starting a second instance\.
.P
Otherwise the script launches \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR under \fBnohup\fR, redirecting both stdout and stderr to a datestamped output file named \fB$RECORD_START_PROGRAM\.<YYYY\-MM\-DD>\.out\fR in the current working directory\. The PID of the background process is written to \fBRECORD_PID_FILE\fR, and a confirmation message is written to standard error\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
This script accepts no options or arguments\. All configuration is supplied via environment variables\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 if \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR is launched successfully\.
.P
Returns \-1 (typically 255) if \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR is already running\.
.P
Returns non\-zero if \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR validation fails at source time (see \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR documentation)\.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR
The program to launch\. Must be set and resolve to an executable on \fBPATH\fR\. Validated by \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR at source time\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR
Used by \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR to construct the PID file path\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_PID_FILE\fR
Path to the PID file, exported by \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR as \fB/tmp/record\.$USER\.$RECORD_DBTYPE\.$RECORD_START_PROGRAM\.pid\fR\. Written with the PID of the launched process on success\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Start a workflow program:
.IP "" 4
.nf
export RECORD_START_PROGRAM=my_sim
export RECORD_DBTYPE=sqlite3
record\-start\.sh
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Start and then monitor for errors:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-start\.sh
sleep 60
record\-errors\.sh
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR
Common library sourced at startup\. Must be present in the working directory or on \fBPATH\fR\.
.TP
\fB/tmp/record\.<USER>\.<RECORD_DBTYPE>\.<RECORD_START_PROGRAM>\.pid\fR
PID file written with the PID of the launched process\. Used by \fBrecord\-stop\.sh\fR, \fBrecord\-edit\.sh\fR, and \fBrecord\-errors\.sh\fR to locate the running process\.
.TP
\fB$RECORD_START_PROGRAM\.<YYYY\-MM\-DD>\.out\fR
Datestamped output file written in the current working directory, capturing both stdout and stderr of the launched process\.
